   "help": "Drop the in→a series resistor R1 and use the 7-part `2LPn-MFB-LS` / 8-part `2LPn-MFB-LS+R7` pair. R1 is the third leg of the (+) divider; without it the DC gain is pinned into a narrow window just under (fz/f0)², so Custom DC gain is switched on and pre-filled with the geometric mean of that window. Any surplus gain or attenuation must then be redistributed to the other stages. Leave unchecked to let the solver pick the R1 pair whenever the target gain falls below the window.",
